    presentation: "63-year-old woman with hypertension and hyperlipidaemia, with CCS class IV angina for 6 months despite maximal beta-blocker and long-acting nitrate. Regadenoson nuclear imaging showed severe inferior ischaemia with normal LV function. Before the procedure: HR 48/min, BP 100/78 mmHg, normal examination, sinus rhythm.",
